        <div id="where-to-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            9. Buying on Amazon vs Buying Direct
          </h2>

          <p>
            Momentous sells mainly through its own site, where the best price is the subscription, about 25 percent off list. The brand also ships 12-serving jars and 10-pack travel sachets, which cost more per gram but let you try a flavor before committing to a full jar.
          </p>

          <p>
            On Amazon, Momentous products appear under titles that sometimes still use the older Essential name. The plant protein, for example, is listed as Momentous Vegan Protein Powder with 20 g of pea and rice protein in a 22-serving tub. Amazon prices can be competitive, and Prime shipping is convenient, but stock and seller details vary by flavor.
          </p>

          <p>
            The main risk with any premium supplement on a marketplace is third-party sellers and old stock. Check that the listing is shipped and sold by Amazon or by the brand's own storefront, check the expiry date when it arrives, and make sure the jar carries the NSF mark. For a drug-tested athlete, matching the lot to the NSF database is worth the extra two minutes.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you are buying more than one jar a month, the direct subscription usually beats Amazon on price. If you are buying a single jar to try, Amazon or a retailer sale is often the cheaper route, and the Check Price buttons above take you to the current Amazon listing.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="skip" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Who Should Skip Momentous
          </h2>

          <p>
            <strong>Budget buyers.</strong> If you are spending your own money and not subject to drug testing, Momentous is hard to justify. A mainstream whey with Informed Choice certification gives you 24 g of protein for less than half the cost per 25 g. Our <a href="/best-whey-protein-powder/">best whey protein powder</a> guide lists the strongest value picks.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>People who want a big scoop.</strong> If you want 30 g or more of protein in one shake, Momentous means a scoop and a half every time, which shortens a 25-serving jar to about 17 shakes and pushes the effective price higher still. Higher-dose isolates make more sense.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Anyone who wants casein or a bedtime protein.</strong> Momentous does not sell a casein powder at the time of writing. If slow-digesting protein before bed is part of your plan, look at our <a href="/best-casein-protein-powder/">best casein protein powder</a> guide instead.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>People with medical conditions.</strong> As with any protein supplement, if you have kidney disease, are pregnant, have allergies or take medication, speak to your doctor or a registered dietitian before adding concentrated protein. Certification confirms what is in the jar; it does not make a product right for every person. Nothing on this page is medical advice.
          </p>

          <p>
            Who should buy it, then? Athletes in NSF-recognized programs, people who want a mild, stevia and monk fruit sweetened isolate with no sucralose, and anyone who values batch-level paperwork enough to pay for it. For those buyers it is one of the two best options available.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing price per scoop instead of per gram</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A 20 g scoop always looks cheaper per serving than a 28 g scoop. Divide the price by total grams of protein in the tub, then multiply by 25, before comparing Momentous with anything else, or you will underestimate what you are paying by a fifth or more.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming every Momentous product is certified the same way</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Certifications apply to specific products and flavors. The whey, plant protein and Recovery all show NSF Certified for Sport on Momentous's pages, but a drug-tested athlete should still check the exact flavor in the NSF database before buying, and recheck when a new limited-edition flavor launches.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying for Recovery when plain whey would do</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Recovery's 10 g of carbohydrate costs a lot per gram of protein. Unless you train twice a day or do long endurance work, the plain isolate plus a piece of fruit or your next meal replaces glycogen just as well for far less money, and you keep control over how much sugar you add.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying from unknown marketplace sellers</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Premium protein is a counterfeit and old-stock target. On Amazon, buy from listings shipped and sold by Amazon or the brand storefront, check the expiry date, and make sure the jar shows the NSF mark before relying on it for competition. Keep the receipt and lot number too.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting the 20 g scoop to cover a big appetite</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                If your plan calls for 30 g or more per shake, one Momentous scoop will not get you there. Use a scoop and a half, accept the shorter jar life, or choose a higher-dose isolate that fits your target in one scoop. Decide before you buy, not halfway through the jar.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

