          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="faq-list">
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Momentous protein powder good?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Yes, for a specific buyer. Momentous Whey Protein Isolate is a clean, NSF Certified for Sport isolate with 20 g of protein in about 90 calories and no sucralose. It is an excellent choice for drug-tested athletes. For everyone else, the small scoop and high price make cheaper certified isolates better value.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>How much protein is in a scoop of Momentous whey?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Momentous lists 20 g of protein per scoop of its grass-fed whey isolate, from about 23.7 to 26.4 g of powder depending on flavor, at the time of writing. That is a smaller serving than most whey brands, which typically deliver 24 to 28 g per scoop, so check how many scoops you need.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Momentous NSF Certified for Sport?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Momentous shows the NSF Certified for Sport mark on its whey isolate, 100% Plant Protein and Recovery product pages at the time of writing. Certification is granted per product and can change, so drug-tested athletes should confirm the exact product and flavor in the NSF Certified for Sport database before buying.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What is the difference between Momentous Essential whey and Whey Protein Isolate?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  They appear to be the same product under an older and a newer name. The brand's current page calls it Whey Protein Isolate, while some retailers and Amazon listings still use Essential Grass-Fed Whey. Both list 20 g of grass-fed whey isolate per scoop with NSF certification, so compare labels rather than names.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Momentous worth the price?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  If you are subject to drug testing, yes: NSF certification and batch paperwork are worth roughly a dollar extra per shake. If you are not, probably not. At about $3.50 per 25 g of protein at list price, it costs far more than mainstream wheys and more than higher-dose certified isolates such as Transparent Labs.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Momentous make a vegan protein powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Yes. Momentous 100% Plant Protein blends PURIS pea protein and organic brown rice protein for 20 g of protein per serving in about 110 to 120 calories, per the label. It is NSF Certified for Sport and vegan per the brand, and each flavor contains about 1 to 2 g of organic cane sugar.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Momentous sold on Amazon?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Momentous products appear on Amazon, sometimes under the older Essential product names, alongside the brand's own website and specialty retailers. Buy from listings shipped and sold by Amazon or the brand storefront, check the expiry date, and confirm the NSF mark. The brand's direct subscription is often cheapest for regular buyers.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

