          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Momentous is a good protein company with a narrow audience. Its whey isolate is clean, mild, NSF Certified for Sport and documented down to the batch, and for a drug-tested athlete that is exactly what a protein powder should be. The 20 g scoop and roughly $3.50 per 25 g of protein at list price are the cost of that assurance.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you are not subject to testing, the money is better spent on a certified isolate with a bigger scoop, or a well-tested mainstream whey. If you are, compare Momentous with Thorne on the day you buy, take the subscription if you will use it every month, and check the NSF database for your flavor before you open the jar.
